From 681fb06cdd094ef091c52d1c4f30523bc21fc552 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 14:31:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Net play: say CLICK, answer beacons both ways, and fix the
 lobby's dead ends

The panel now says what to press, on every line that wants it. Rows read
[CLICK] 192.168.1.23  online / not heard yet; the header says CLICK the
other pc below to connect; the host sees [ CLICK HERE TO START ] with a
line explaining < > then START; the client is told the host clicks START
and there is nothing to click here. The address prompt is drawn on the
panel itself, in its place, rather than in yellow in the corner behind it.

The "no answer on the non-host" case: beacons went by broadcast plus a
unicast to every TYPED-IN address, so typing the host's address on the
joining pc made the host hear the joiner - but the joiner still only had
the host's broadcast to go on, which is the thing the router was dropping.
Now every machine we have heard from gets a unicast beacon too, so one
typed address on either side fills both lists.

Lobby dead ends fixed: the host's clickmap sat on top of the peer list
(START ate the third row); the both-picked tie-break was tested while the
role was still off, which it never is by then; a dropped connection before
a game marked the session dead and left the panel unusable; EXIT as a
lobby host started mission 1 through F7's auto-start; quitting to the menu
used net_fail and left the role set, so NET PLAY could not be used twice
without restarting; the client never closed its lobby in-game; a second
copy on one pc that cannot bind UDP 6511 now still shouts from an unbound
socket so the first copy lists it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016FwDFgMbTFdYGVdwP6Bi4Q
